{:edb/db-before-t 2826 :edb/db-after-t 2827 :edb/tx-data [[13194139536139 50 #inst "2026-10-09T16:36:25.101Z" 13194139536139 true] [17592186114987 1100 "Consider the system of linear equations\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042553/assets/a50d551e5d8abe8d9ae48778b195c382bbbf96f6fc5083c41b67642e99deffda.png)\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." 13194139536139 false] [17592186114987 1100 "Consider the system of linear equations\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079703/assets/a50d551e5d8abe8d9ae48778b195c382bbbf96f6fc5083c41b67642e99deffda.png)\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." 13194139536139 true] [17592186114987 1145 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042553/assets/48c423256fbdc0d7e4f6ff716fb449efe6f98bdf57ba90353bcced930ea4ed17.png)\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 2 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042553/assets/81b7626ac30b06c5eeb10be274dd93476a86dce5fe3053722d96e16b78d7f165.png)\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $z,$ and we have one free variable, $y.$ That means we need to find $x$ and $z$ in terms of $y.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-1-5y \\\\ y=y \\\\ z=3,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1-5y \\\\ y \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536139 false] [17592186114987 1145 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079703/assets/48c423256fbdc0d7e4f6ff716fb449efe6f98bdf57ba90353bcced930ea4ed17.png)\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 2 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079703/assets/81b7626ac30b06c5eeb10be274dd93476a86dce5fe3053722d96e16b78d7f165.png)\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $z,$ and we have one free variable, $y.$ That means we need to find $x$ and $z$ in terms of $y.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-1-5y \\\\ y=y \\\\ z=3,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1-5y \\\\ y \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536139 true] [17592186114988 1145 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042553/assets/a115d3da691619918bf92d914acdfdd95088e9a141a82ca3fe3230fa7fbb8172.png)\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & k & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & k+4 & -5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042553/assets/cfea36ae2b5cb5d8715480c1e0ee0b5ba06cf39d0c2032eb6e9b9078bf8c5bde.png)\n\nThe system is inconsistent if it has no solutions. For the system to have no solutions, one of the equations above must be false.\n\nIf $k=-4,$ then the second equation is $0=-5,$ which is false, and the system will have no solution.\n\nTherefore, our system is inconsistent when $k=-4.$" 13194139536139 false] [17592186114988 1145 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079703/assets/f4478e5828da7c79a47bf3ca212ed15357befe7b0b208c78beb0895b445272c9.png)\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & k & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & k+4 & -5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079703/assets/cfea36ae2b5cb5d8715480c1e0ee0b5ba06cf39d0c2032eb6e9b9078bf8c5bde.png)\n\nThe system is inconsistent if it has no solutions. For the system to have no solutions, one of the equations above must be false.\n\nIf $k=-4,$ then the second equation is $0=-5,$ which is false, and the system will have no solution.\n\nTherefore, our system is inconsistent when $k=-4.$" 13194139536139 true] [17592186115041 1100 "Given the system\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042553/assets/5f1aaf29a3dd8b7ea2c4f7104d532f7b56f32a23ccebbcfa0d1bfe86c772cc5f.png)\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- The system is consistent dependent\n\n- The system has no solution\n\n- The system is consistent independent" 13194139536139 false] [17592186115041 1100 "Given the system\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079703/assets/427c19efbebba6bfe2dc36bccd852d7a1f5e0ec97dc46c00043d019807e86ec2.png)\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- The system is consistent dependent\n\n- The system has no solution\n\n- The system is consistent independent" 13194139536139 true] [17592186115041 1145 "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042553/assets/6171d242b0a3887802f629de79cb952d47711a581e88db2d9304a5db356dfb62.png)\n\nUsing Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 6 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042553/assets/80aff0fd62e3e1aeed17017c864d8d0b875b556ce1a29a89e6c61e632bf9c733.png)\n\nSince any numbers $x$ and $y$ form a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of just a single equation:\n\n$$\n2x -3y= 4\n$$\n\nThe basic variable is $x,$ and we have a free variable $y.$ That means we need to find $x$ in terms of $y.$ \n\nTherefore, since there are infinitely many solutions, we conclude that the system is *consistent dependent*.\n\nAs a result, only statement I is true." 13194139536139 false] [17592186115041 1145 "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079703/assets/50f13deaa03c2af30f511ef3d514e3dd2e118d81d9b121b436ff1a2f2497c303.png)\n\nUsing Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 6 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079703/assets/e02bb5004f792eea20216e64098bb924dbed15defb9330967d6ae5a144e067dc.png)\n\nSince any numbers $x$ and $y$ form a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of just a single equation:\n\n$$\n2x -3y= 4\n$$\n\nThe basic variable is $x,$ and we have a free variable $y.$ That means we need to find $x$ in terms of $y.$ \n\nTherefore, since there are infinitely many solutions, we conclude that the system is *consistent dependent*.\n\nAs a result, only statement I is true." 13194139536139 true] [17592186115161 1020 #edb/ref 17592186385567 13194139536139 true] [17592186115161 1020 #edb/ref 17592186385595 13194139536139 true] [17592186115161 1020 #edb/ref 17592186385609 13194139536139 true] [17592186115162 1020 #edb/ref 17592186385581 13194139536139 true] [17592186115162 1020 #edb/ref 17592186385588 13194139536139 true] [17592186115162 1020 #edb/ref 17592186385602 13194139536139 true] [17592186115162 1020 #edb/ref 17592186385630 13194139536139 true] [17592186115219 1020 #edb/ref 17592186385574 13194139536139 true] [17592186115219 1020 #edb/ref 17592186385616 13194139536139 true] [17592186115219 1020 #edb/ref 17592186385623 13194139536139 true] [17592186115671 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536139 true] [17592186115671 1100 "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{  \\begin{array}{rl} & - x + 2 y = 6 \\\\  & 2 x - 3 y = 13 \\\\  & 5 x - y = 45\\end{array} \\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n1. The system is consistent dependent\n2. The system is inconsistent\n3. The system has a unique solution" 13194139536139 false] [17592186115671 1100 "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & -x+2y=6 \\\\  & 2x-3y=13 \\\\  & 5x-y=45\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- The system is consistent dependent\n- The system is inconsistent\n- The system has a unique solution" 13194139536139 true] [17592186115671 1145 "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 13 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 45\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 13 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 45\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 25 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 45\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 25 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 75\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-9){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 25 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -150\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe final row corresponds to the equation $0x+0y=-150,$ and this has no solution. Therefore, our system has no solution, and we conclude that the system is inconsistent.\n\nAs a result, only statement II is true." 13194139536139 true] [17592186385567 1017 #edb/ref 17592186385568 13194139536139 true] [17592186385567 1089 "q-131715" 13194139536139 true] [17592186385567 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536139 true] [17592186385567 1100 "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=2 \\\\ {x}_{1}-3{x}_{3}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." 13194139536139 true] [17592186385567 1113 #uuid "0f67dc1c-a8f3-5dc9-a4b3-b289bc053549" 13194139536139 true] [17592186385567 1145 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe corresponding system is now  \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & {x}_{1}-3{x}_{3}=1 \\\\  & {x}_{2}-5{x}_{3}=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2},$ and we have one free variable, ${x}_{3}.$ That means we need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ in terms of ${x}_{3}.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}=3{x}_{3}+1 \\\\ {x}_{2}=5{x}_{3}-1 \\\\ {x}_{3}={x}_{3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{3}$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{3}+1 \\\\ 5{x}_{3}-1 \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536139 true] [17592186385568 1000 #edb/ref 17592186385569 13194139536139 true] [17592186385568 1000 #edb/ref 17592186385570 13194139536139 true] [17592186385568 1000 #edb/ref 17592186385571 13194139536139 true] [17592186385568 1000 #edb/ref 17592186385572 13194139536139 true] [17592186385568 1000 #edb/ref 17592186385573 13194139536139 true] [17592186385568 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536139 true] [17592186385568 1041 "selection" 13194139536139 true] [17592186385568 1104 #edb/ref 17592186385572 13194139536139 true] [17592186385568 1110 #uuid "917e81fc-fd40-5388-84ae-8fd66738e6b1" 13194139536139 true] [17592186385569 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{3}-1 \\\\ 5{x}_{3}+1 \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139536139 true] [17592186385569 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536139 true] [17592186385569 1111 #uuid "20d7bbd4-4dcd-5f2c-a52d-4451d28a9855" 13194139536139 true] [17592186385570 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}1-3{x}_{3} \\\\ 1-5{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139536139 true] [17592186385570 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536139 true] [17592186385570 1111 #uuid "909c2fa2-18bb-56f6-a07f-ffbd60e70395" 13194139536139 true] [17592186385571 1034 "No solution" 13194139536139 true] [17592186385571 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536139 true] [17592186385571 1111 #uuid "8230423a-b173-5e28-a487-08578c77c8ce" 13194139536139 true] [17592186385572 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{3}+1 \\\\ 5{x}_{3}-1 \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139536139 true] [17592186385572 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536139 true] [17592186385572 1111 #uuid "78e22ea5-4a2a-5074-807e-b38670f29eb6" 13194139536139 true] [17592186385573 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{3}+1 \\\\ 1-5{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139536139 true] [17592186385573 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536139 true] [17592186385573 1111 #uuid "e44c7a57-9f6f-57ab-a0d0-44cc92029548" 13194139536139 true] [17592186385574 1017 #edb/ref 17592186385575 13194139536139 true] [17592186385574 1089 "q-131723" 13194139536139 true] [17592186385574 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536139 true] [17592186385574 1100 "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x-y+z=3 \\\\  & -3x+3y-3z=10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- The system is inconsistent\n- The system has a unique solution\n- The system is consistent dependent" 13194139536139 true] [17592186385574 1113 #uuid "0683e131-d27c-52ac-9ea2-e2395865251d" 13194139536139 true] [17592186385574 1145 "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 3 & -3 & 10\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 3 & -3 & 10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 19\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe final row corresponds to the equation $0x+0y+0z=19,$ and this has no solution. Therefore, our system has no solution, and we conclude that the system is inconsistent.\n\nAs a result, only statement I is true." 13194139536139 true] [17592186385575 1000 #edb/ref 17592186385576 13194139536139 true] [17592186385575 1000 #edb/ref 17592186385577 13194139536139 true] [17592186385575 1000 #edb/ref 17592186385578 13194139536139 true] [17592186385575 1000 #edb/ref 17592186385579 13194139536139 true] [17592186385575 1000 #edb/ref 17592186385580 13194139536139 true] [17592186385575 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536139 true] [17592186385575 1041 "selection" 13194139536139 true] [17592186385575 1104 #edb/ref 17592186385577 13194139536139 true] [17592186385575 1110 #uuid "f0c6ce4e-208b-5270-84b0-c69fca8d4c92" 13194139536139 true] [17592186385576 1034 "II and III only" 13194139536139 true] [17592186385576 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536139 true] [17592186385576 1111 #uuid "d8903f11-0cba-58d2-be49-cac41448500a" 13194139536139 true] [17592186385577 1034 "I only" 13194139536139 true] [17592186385577 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536139 true] [17592186385577 1111 #uuid "fb4b9a6b-af1a-5623-a24c-5b1ad6705419" 13194139536139 true] [17592186385578 1034 "III only" 13194139536139 true] [17592186385578 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536139 true] [17592186385578 1111 #uuid "4339f9f5-91ec-5c96-8cf9-fc8bdef769b6" 13194139536139 true] [17592186385579 1034 "None" 13194139536139 true] [17592186385579 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536139 true] [17592186385579 1111 #uuid "7fcb2f4a-73fa-58f0-a9e0-167d0c8521ec" 13194139536139 true] [17592186385580 1034 "II only" 13194139536139 true] [17592186385580 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536139 true] [17592186385580 1111 #uuid "a2223ece-52c7-5aa8-9edb-669f38312dc8" 13194139536139 true] [17592186385581 1017 #edb/ref 17592186385582 13194139536139 true] [17592186385581 1089 "q-131728" 13194139536139 true] [17592186385581 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536139 true] [17592186385581 1100 "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is inconsistent:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & -x+4y=-2 \\\\  & -3x+(3k+15)y=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536139 true] [17592186385581 1113 #uuid "dc0a4fe5-74aa-50e7-beb1-354fa029945a" 13194139536139 true] [17592186385581 1145 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 3k+15 & -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 3k+15 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3k+3 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-x+4y=-2 \\\\ (3k+3)y=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is inconsistent if it has no solutions. For the system to have no solutions, one of the equations above must be false.\n\nIf $k=-1,$ then the second equation is $0=2,$ which is false, and the system will have no solution.\n\nTherefore, our system is inconsistent when $k=-1.$" 13194139536139 true] [17592186385582 1000 #edb/ref 17592186385583 13194139536139 true] [17592186385582 1000 #edb/ref 17592186385584 13194139536139 true] [17592186385582 1000 #edb/ref 17592186385585 13194139536139 true] [17592186385582 1000 #edb/ref 17592186385586 13194139536139 true] [17592186385582 1000 #edb/ref 17592186385587 13194139536139 true] [17592186385582 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536139 true] [17592186385582 1041 "selection" 13194139536139 true] [17592186385582 1104 #edb/ref 17592186385586 13194139536139 true] [17592186385582 1110 #uuid "f4a82629-076c-55ed-87f4-03609f626ead" 13194139536139 true] [17592186385583 1034 "k=-2" 13194139536139 true] [17592186385583 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536139 true] [17592186385583 1111 #uuid "c13a8f7e-82f0-53ac-9688-c35a2cf68ceb" 13194139536139 true] [17592186385584 1034 "k=1" 13194139536139 true] [17592186385584 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536139 true] [17592186385584 1111 #uuid "6f410d1e-ecab-5375-beb3-384d5f377665" 13194139536139 true] [17592186385585 1034 "k=2" 13194139536139 true] [17592186385585 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536139 true] [17592186385585 1111 #uuid "a5853016-6db8-5d71-b85b-ba03606577be" 13194139536139 true] [17592186385586 1034 "k=-1" 13194139536139 true] [17592186385586 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536139 true] [17592186385586 1111 #uuid "91bc9db8-f764-53dc-b349-1b457d68b0c7" 13194139536139 true] [17592186385587 1034 "k=0" 13194139536139 true] [17592186385587 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536139 true] [17592186385587 1111 #uuid "5db4c8bd-c840-5d2f-92ae-f598d638c7c4" 13194139536139 true] [17592186385588 1017 #edb/ref 17592186385589 13194139536139 true] [17592186385588 1089 "q-32245" 13194139536139 true] [17592186385588 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536139 true] [17592186385588 1100 "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is inconsistent:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 2x-y=3 \\\\  & 4x+ky=4\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536139 true] [17592186385588 1113 #uuid "376102dd-bbbf-5006-9d2c-7f1bfeb57afa" 13194139536139 true] [17592186385588 1145 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 4 & k & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 4 & k & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & k+2 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 2x-y=3 \\\\  & (k+2)y=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is inconsistent if it has no solutions. For the system to have no solutions, one of the equations above must be false.\n\nNow if $k=-2$, then the second equation is $0=-2,$ which is false, and the system will have no solution.\n\nTherefore, our system is inconsistent when  $k=-2.$" 13194139536139 true] [17592186385589 1000 #edb/ref 17592186385590 13194139536139 true] [17592186385589 1000 #edb/ref 17592186385591 13194139536139 true] [17592186385589 1000 #edb/ref 17592186385592 13194139536139 true] [17592186385589 1000 #edb/ref 17592186385593 13194139536139 true] [17592186385589 1000 #edb/ref 17592186385594 13194139536139 true] [17592186385589 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536139 true] [17592186385589 1041 "selection" 13194139536139 true] [17592186385589 1104 #edb/ref 17592186385590 13194139536139 true] [17592186385589 1110 #uuid "590002f2-d7a2-5ecd-9881-510b1a3b5477" 13194139536139 true] [17592186385590 1034 "k=-2" 13194139536139 true] [17592186385590 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 131941395