1}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 10 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -6 & 6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe corresponding system is now  \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & {x}_{1}+10{x}_{3}=-8 \\\\  & {x}_{2}-6{x}_{3}=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2},$ and we have one free variable, ${x}_{3}.$ That means we need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ in terms of ${x}_{3}.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}=-8-10{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2}=6+6{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}={x}_{3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{3}$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-8-10{x}_{3} \\\\ 6+6{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536139 true] [17592186385596 1000 #edb/ref 17592186385597 13194139536139 true] [17592186385596 1000 #edb/ref 17592186385598 13194139536139 true] [17592186385596 1000 #edb/ref 17592186385599 13194139536139 true] [17592186385596 1000 #edb/ref 17592186385600 13194139536139 true] [17592186385596 1000 #edb/ref 17592186385601 13194139536139 true] [17592186385596 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536139 true] [17592186385596 1041 "selection" 13194139536139 true] [17592186385596 1104 #edb/ref 17592186385597 13194139536139 true] [17592186385596 1110 #uuid "19546a12-a85b-5327-a3e4-e7420e808b8f" 13194139536139 true] [17592186385597 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}-8-10{x}_{3} \\\\ 6+6{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139536139 true] [17592186385597 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536139 true] [17592186385597 1111 #uuid "967daa91-b36c-5199-a6dd-973438d43f0f" 13194139536139 true] [17592186385598 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}8-{x}_{3} \\\\ 3+3{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]